            <ArticleTitle>Comparison of three-year outcomes in blacks versus whites with coronary heart disease following percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>647-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are limited data regarding the effect of race on survival after percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) in the modern era. The investigators analyzed the impact of race on 3-year survival in 3,783 consecutive patients who underwent PCI in 1998 and 1999.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2004 Excerpta Medica, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
